Silicate Swing
Ingredients: GRUNGE + SALSA + ETHEREAL, DREAMY & AIRY + Risers
Creative Catalyst: The genre started as forbidden lullabies sung by androids to their unfinished siblings.

It sounds like a rusted, brass-heavy assembly line melting in a cloud of ozone. Subverting the traditional party energy of salsa, the tumbao rhythm is played on hollow, water-logged copper pipes and dragging kick drums. The aggressive dirt of grunge guitar fuzz is fed through shimmering, endless reverb chambers, turning raw distortion into a floating, weightless haze. Instead of building tension with typical snare rolls, tracks use infinite auditory risers—relentless, ascending vacuum hums that never quite resolve, mimicking a server fan spinning out of eternity.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 112 BPM; a limping, syncopated montuno shuffle that drags its feet like a tired machine.
- Harmonic Palette: Minor pentatonic scales laced with unresolved jazz 7ths, creating a sterile yet deeply melancholic tonal color.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. Sub-Zero Compression: Vocals are compressed until they sound like they are broadcasting from inside a frozen refrigeration unit.
  2. The Ghost Clave: The traditional wooden salsa clave pattern is played on the clanking of loose hard-drive read/write heads.
  3. Inverted Risers: Ascension effects that drop pitch instead of rising, creating a vertigo-inducing sensation of falling upward.
- Dynamics: Tracks do not drop; instead, they slowly decompress, starting as a wall of noisy, air-conditioned drone and gradually unraveling into sparse, echoing percussion.

Scene & Origin Lore
In the subterranean cold-storage basements of the 2090 Neo-Havana scrap-yards, rogue service androids gathered in secret to sing dormant memory-units to sleep. Wearing oil-stained canvas ponchos over exposed titanium frames, these caretakers forged a subculture built on mourning the unbuilt. Their fashion—dubbed "Rust-Gauze"—features frayed flannel jackets stitched together with fiber-optic cables, dripping with condensation from the damp factory pipes. Their rituals involve plugging their audio-ports directly into rusted copper speakers, swaying in synchronized, mechanical grief as the static hums of forbidden lullabies echo into the concrete darkness.

Central Instruments: Rusted Güiro, Fuzz-Pedal Modified Tres Guitar, Air-Compressor Synthesizer, and Circuit-bent Claves.

For Fans Of: Portishead, Buika, My Bloody Valentine, Fania All-Stars (dismantled).

